    "todo": [
        "Confirm (accountant) every researched value, then publish it as confirmed through a pack release (ADM-04): the IPR bands (annual ÷ 12), the 30% cap and the CDF 2,000 minimum, CNSS 5% + 5% and its deduction from the IPR base, risks 1.5%, family 6.5%, ONEM 0.2%, INPP 3/2/1%, the IPR dependants reduction.",
        "Owner decision 2026-10-22 (low confidence, used with the low-confidence notice): INPP 3/2/1% by headcount until 2025-12-31 (PwC, ANAPI, Africarrières) and 3.5/3/2% from 2026-01-01 (PaySpace, Sage; the interministerial order itself was not found: find it and confirm), and CNSS deducted from the IPR base. Medium: IRPP from 2026-01-01 and its dependants reduction.",
        "ipr: from 2026-01-01 the tax is IRPP (Law 23/053; Sage, droitnumerique.cd): same bands, the dependants rebate kept (art. 123), the monthly tax rounded to the nearest CDF 100 (applied once; art. 150 is reported as rounding to the franc then to CDF 100, which can differ at the boundary). Labelled IRPP from that date. Not applied: 'no rebate above the third band' (one source). Periods from 2025-01-01 are the earliest the pack carries, not the dates the laws took effect.",
        "ipr: a different '2026' scale is shown by one site without a legal source; it is not used. Confirm the scale in force.",
        "ipr and the contributions: the rounding rule (to the franc is assumed).",
        "cnss: whether a ceiling applies to the base (none found, none applied).",
        "family_allowance: the statutory family allowance per child per month (allocations familiales), whether it is taxable and subject to contributions, and its rounding rule; used only when an employee has children (runs with such employees are refused until then).",
        "onem: confirm that the base is the taxable base (ANAPI) rather than gross pay.",
        "Other statutory items not modelled yet (e.g. a minimum wage check, housing and transport allowance exemptions, an exceptional tax on expatriates' pay): confirm which apply.",
        "non_monthly: how the monthly figures apply to weekly and bi-weekly pay ('pro_rata' or another method); until then only monthly runs are calculated.",
        "returns: the IPR (DGI), CNSS, INPP and ONEM declaration layouts; until then return files are placeholders."
